<DocsLayout
  slug="ota-installs"
  title="Installing staging builds"
  description="Ad Hoc install links for staging builds, and how long they stick around."
>
  <h2 id="the-install-link">The install link</h2>
  <p>
    Once a staging build finishes, pkgr.app hosts the signed artifact itself and shows an
    "Install" button on the build's detail page. Open that page on the target device to install
    over the air — no cable, no store submission. Production builds aren't hosted this way; see
    below.
  </p>

  <h2 id="artifact-retention">Artifact retention</h2>
  <p>
    Hosted staging artifacts are kept for a plan-based window, then deleted automatically: 7 days
    on Free, 30 on Starter, 90 on Pro, unlimited on Enterprise. The build detail page shows
    "Available until &lt;date&gt;" while it's live. Once that date passes, the install button
    reverts to its default state — trigger a new build to get a fresh, installable artifact.
  </p>

  <h2 id="production-artifacts">Production artifacts</h2>
  <p>
    Production builds aren't copied into pkgr.app's own storage — they exist only as the GitHub
    Actions run's artifact, subject to GitHub's own retention window. Download the signed binary
    from the build's detail page while that underlying artifact is still available on GitHub's
    side.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
